  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:fixed-a-endpoint-frontier",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Fix \\(\\eta\\in\\mathcal C(\\mathcal O)\\), \\(k\\in[K]\\), and an intervention-created observed adjacency \\(uv\\), where \\(u,v\\in A(\\eta)\\), \\(uv\\notin H\\), and \\(uv\\) is present in the regime-\\(k\\) skeleton. Let \\(e\\) be the endpoint at \\(u\\) on \\(uv\\). Then\n\\[\n \\varnothing\\ne\\mathcal M_A(e;\\mathcal O,\\eta)\n \\subseteq \\mathcal G_A(u,v;k).\n\\]\nThus, if \\(u\\notin Z_k\\), then \\(\\mathcal M_A(e;\\mathcal O,\\eta)=\\{\\mathtt{tail}\\}\\); if \\(u\\in Z_k\\) and \\(\\operatorname{Reach}_{A(\\eta)}(u,v)=0\\), then \\(\\mathcal M_A(e;\\mathcal O,\\eta)=\\{\\mathtt{arrow}\\}\\). If \\(u\\in Z_k\\) and \\(\\operatorname{Reach}_{A(\\eta)}(u,v)=1\\), the empty graph \\(B_0\\) on \\(A(\\eta)\\) and the directed-edge graph \\(B_P\\) of any simple \\(u\\)-to-\\(v\\) path in \\(L_{A(\\eta)}\\) are admissible and give two common-basal graphical replacement specifications preserving \\(A(\\eta)\\) and every regime skeleton and unshielded collider on the full domains \\(U_j\\). The former has an arrowhead and the latter a tail at \\(e\\). In this two-mark case,\n\\[\n \\operatorname{Real}(\\eta,B_0)\\ne\\varnothing\n \\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n \\operatorname{Real}(\\eta,B_P)\\ne\\varnothing\n \\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n \\mathcal M_A(e;\\mathcal O,\\eta)=\\mathcal G_A(u,v;k)\n =\\{\\mathtt{tail},\\mathtt{arrow}\\}.\n\\]\nHere \\(u\\in Z_k\\) denotes direct targeting or indirect affectedness within \\(A(\\eta)\\), not necessarily \\(u\\in T_k(\\eta)\\). Retained adjacencies \\(uv\\in H\\) are outside this intervention-created-edge bracket.",
