    "justification": "The corrected theorem proves the faithful-model outer bracket, exact singleton cases, and two graphical specifications for the two-mark case.",
    "gap": "Two-mark equality needs both corresponding faithful realization fibers to be nonempty.",
    "consumer": "It distinguishes already identified fixed-\\(A\\) endpoints from ambiguity that remains only graphical until faithful promotion.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(g=\\operatorname{gr}(\\eta)\\).  By \\(\\mathrm{lem:exact\\mbox{-}fixed\\mbox{-}a\\mbox{-}graphical\\mbox{-}frontier}\\),\n\\[\n \\varnothing\\ne\\mathcal M_A(e;\\mathcal O,\\eta)\n \\subseteq\\mathcal M_A^{\\mathrm{gr}}(e;\\mathcal O,g)\n =\\mathcal G_A(u,v;k).\n\\tag{1}\n\\]\nDiscarding the middle term proves the required nonempty inclusion.  In either singleton case in the definition of \\(\\mathcal G_A\\), a nonempty subset of that singleton equals it, so (1) gives the two asserted law-level identifications.\n\nIf \\(u\\in Z_k\\) and \\(\\operatorname{Reach}_{A(\\eta)}(u,v)=1\\), the same lemma proves that \\(B_0\\) and every simple-path graph \\(B_P\\) are admissible; their replacement specifications preserve \\(A(\\eta)\\) and the complete graphical signature on every \\(U_j\\), and their marks at \\(e\\) are respectively \\(\\mathtt{arrow}\\) and \\(\\mathtt{tail}\\).  If both displayed realization fibers are nonempty, \\(\\mathrm{lem:replacement\\mbox{-}preservation}\\) promotes one member of each fiber, not the bare graphical specifications themselves, into \\(\\mathcal C_A(\\mathcal O,\\eta)\\).  The two opposite marks then belong to \\(\\mathcal M_A(e;\\mathcal O,\\eta)\\); (1) and the two-element definition of \\(\\mathcal G_A\\) give the asserted equality.  The interpretation of \\(Z_k\\) follows from the indicator-neighbor identity, and the exclusion of retained adjacencies is certified by \\(\\mathrm{prop:retained\\mbox{-}edge\\mbox{-}sanity\\mbox{-}reduction}\\). \\(\\square\\)",
